<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sin-muballit</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sin-muballit was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> and the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi">Hammurabi</a>. He was the last of the five rulers who built Babylon into a regional power. The Babylonian Empire profile credits these kings with completing city walls and infrastructure.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sin-muballit.jpg" alt="Sin-muballit" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osama Shukir Muhammed Amin FRCP(Glasg) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clay_tablet_and_its_sealed_clay_envelope._Legal_document,_listing_of_land_and_their_distribution_to_several_sons._From_Sippar,_Iraq._Old-Babylonian_period._Reign_of_Sin-Muballit,_1812-1793_BCE._Vorderasiatisches_Museum,_Berlin,_Germany.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
